  "headline": "Stilly Buys Last Year's Rushing Champion",
  "publicationDraft": "Stilly paired McCaffrey with the reigning rushing champion, sending Barkley and Thielen to Mitch. Taylor was still valued above Barkley in contemporary rankings, but Barkley's 194-yard Week 1 resurgence was already public knowledge. Taylor's recurring ankle injuries wrecked the investment, culminating in a Week 15 exit against Minnesota. That same week Mitch beat Stilly 127.90–94.92, with Barkley and Thielen supplying 32.10 and Taylor just 1.80. Mitch's acquisitions stayed useful into December. Stilly's bet on elite talent was understandable, but paying a starting receiver to upgrade a resurgent Barkley was a costly gamble. Mitch bought two starters; Stilly bought last year's headlines.",
